  "explanation_track_count_change": "Explanation of Track Count Shift (48 -> 26 tracks):\nUnder the earlier permissive gate ('evidence >= 1.5s OR margin >= 0.15'), 48 tracks met the gate\nand unlocked live names; their frame counts were aggregated into student totals, totaling 484.57 person-seconds.\nUnder the strict dual gate ('BOTH margin >= 0.15 AND evidence >= 1.5s'), 22 tracks failed to meet\nboth gates simultaneously. Because the previous reporting script only mapped track_to_assigned_person\nwhen pid in KNOWN_STUDENTS, those 22 tracks were completely omitted from student frame sums.\nThis caused counted tracks to drop from 48 to 26 and enrolled person-seconds to drop from 484.57s to 450.30s\n(the 34.27s from those 22 tracks was excluded). Under the redesigned gate, candidate tracking\nand retroactive relabeling cleanly attribute these tracks, eliminating artificial denominator loss."
